{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-0111"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Cereal-Growing Operations Coordination"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "0111"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :agriculture/cereal-growing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:food-security :rural-employment :environmental-stewardship]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :field-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :audit-ledger]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies [:telemetry :optimization :dmn :bpmn]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "CerealOpsAdvisor ⊣ Field Operations Governor, langgraph-clj
 StateGraph (langgraph.graph, cerealops.operation/build), append-only
 audit ledger (cerealops.store/ledger + append-ledger!, MemStore and a
 DatomicStore backed by langchain.db via langchain-store.core). A
 back-office OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for cereal-growing field
 management (wheat/maize/barley/sorghum/oats/rye/millet) -- not direct
 field-equipment operation authority and not
 pesticide-application-decision authority. Four ops
 (`:log-field-record` / `:schedule-field-operation` /
 `:flag-crop-health-concern` / `:order-supplies`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Five HARD invariants (field-not-registered,
 no-execution, equipment-or-pesticide-decision-blocked, op-not-allowed,
 field-record-invalid) plus independent cost/acreage/confidence
 verification (`cerealops.registry`) elaborate this blueprint's
 Governor. Crop-health-concern flagging ALWAYS escalates to a human
 farmer/agronomist via the compiled graph's `:request-approval` node
 (`interrupt-before`, checkpoint-based resume); `:log-field-record` and
 `:schedule-field-operation` are the ops eligible to auto-commit, and
 only at phase 3 when the Governor is clean. Every commit/hold/
 approval-rejected decision lands in the append-only ledger -- 32
 tests / 105 assertions green (`clojure -M:dev:test`), demo runnable
 end-to-end against both Store backends (`clojure -M:dev:run`)."}
